# Normalise line endings in the repository, check them out as the platform expects.
#
# This does not rewrite anything that is already committed. Adding it stops the
# next commit from carrying a whole-file line ending change for a one line edit,
# which is what makes a diff unreadable. Files already in the tree keep whatever
# they have until something touches them deliberately, so this is a change to how
# things behave from here on, not a reformat of the past.
#
# To actually normalise everything that is already committed, which is a separate
# decision and a separate review, run:
#   git add --renormalize .
# and commit that on its own. Do not fold it into a change that does something.

* text=auto

# Anything FxSound or Windows wants to see byte for byte, byte for byte.
*.ico   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.png   binary
*.gif   binary
*.mp3   binary
*.bin   binary
*.exe   binary
*.fac   text eol=crlf
